db/id "q-331891/field-3/a7a1ac5834a653d4d025968e77fa3deeaa5432014068e05f98aec0cb8f2c463b" :answer/id #uuid "6debdc4f-0cab-5492-9401-1afb51beb8a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2}(s)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331891/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "91a7110e-0144-58cb-8d97-0fa86a7be0df" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-331891/field-3/a7a1ac5834a653d4d025968e77fa3deeaa5432014068e05f98aec0cb8f2c463b" :answer-field/choices ["q-331891/field-3/477b09a1a38f7201ccdb3ccc322e142a8878e78314064d5fddf92bb8371e98b5" "q-331891/field-3/be101f3da89332d397adc6f8e793d967f644829103e22e4952aff97fd5ae5222" "q-331891/field-3/ba17edf34a0b129e6602764b7b8858cf47cff0e1272b9ed5d6f9f614d090f550" "q-331891/field-3/a7a1ac5834a653d4d025968e77fa3deeaa5432014068e05f98aec0cb8f2c463b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331891" :question/id #uuid "a2771b9b-89bc-5a83-829a-af6b6b2d190a" :question/math-academy-id "q-331891" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}=-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ {{field-2}}={{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}-4L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-7=-3{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331891/field-1" "q-331891/field-2" "q-331891/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd7b8fc8-26d3-5551-9a46-45725bd863a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331907/field-1/543e2480a1a957bff3396931ee69708823473db1413a74bfe4420304eb702da5" :answer/id #uuid "286229f1-95af-5d1d-aab8-3ffb3066e1aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331907/field-1/d1691a97537efbf1b99a7abaebbda2887fa747e38d89ee390ac0d71887d3a4cd" :answer/id #uuid "83d97a14-7e8d-5e50-a7c9-956c51e8854e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331907/field-1/6118a63ccf34587603e5ff2a08431564393f26c7aea425ce133b4f3ae9d4e92f" :answer/id #uuid "b7459ecb-9cf7-558a-a961-a1f4978e7e0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331907/field-1/1241ae73a34fe86d0a8f2dbfaa305854d671fd4eb7c19592d2e044e29f8d7497" :answer/id #uuid "8c2b86a7-ba71-5e87-b432-2fcd208949ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331907/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6825985a-a3e1-5b7c-93bf-3cd8d5b3470f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-331907/field-1/1241ae73a34fe86d0a8f2dbfaa305854d671fd4eb7c19592d2e044e29f8d7497" :answer-field/choices ["q-331907/field-1/543e2480a1a957bff3396931ee69708823473db1413a7