f each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}} \\\\ {{field-3}}=2{X}_{1}(s)+6{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{3{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L{{x}_{1}(t)}-4L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+6L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2=3{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-5=2{X}_{1}(s)+6{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331907/field-1" "q-331907/field-2" "q-331907/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd7b8fc8-26d3-5551-9a46-45725bd863a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331892/field-1/42aace6deedc993ecc3259eba1a23f09fc1136a37def8d2f9ef749a6e1dd80d1" :answer/id #uuid "d15d66a0-4dee-5dc5-bd98-79aa80e870c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331892/field-1/b20382d842ace3c8595b6bc7e14516923525b1b867139a78b5b3b530c53b4bb6" :answer/id #uuid "61c1cd58-b623-5896-ad41-91a42b446a76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331892/field-1/33559c69d95a124856fd884b6a39b466978e5e7a3aa2d2c8a58d71994abb